  "kind": "project",
  "name": "Bug tracker",
  "publisher": "Initiative",
  "description": "Reports come in, get sorted, get fixed. In that order, ideally.",
  "long_description": "New bugs land in Triage, where somebody decides how bad each one is before it goes to the Backlog. From there it is In progress, In review and Done, or Won't fix for the ones that are really features.\n\nEvery report has a severity, the part of the product it is in, the version it was found in and whether anyone has made it happen twice. Severity says how bad it is for the person who hit it. Priority says when you will get to it. They are allowed to disagree.\n\nNot everything is a bug. Feature requests get a page that is mostly the conversation, and chores, like the upgrade nobody asked for, get a plain one.",
  "avatar_url": "/marketplace/core-bug-tracker.svg",
  "images": [],
  "version": "1.2.0",
  "release_notes": "Bugs, feature requests and chores are each their own type, with a page of their own. A new bug starts with steps to reproduce, and a card shows its type beside its title. The project's fields are its own properties rather than the initiative's metadata.",
